OpenIMP licensing notice
========================

OpenIMP is an open implementation of Ingenic's libimp API.  The project
has no single project-wide license file yet.  Licensing is per file:

1. Files with an SPDX-License-Identifier or license header are under that
   license.  At the time of writing:

   - LGPL-2.1-or-later: include/openimp/openimp_avc.h,
     src/t40/openimp_avc.c, src/t40/openimp_core_lease.h, src/jpeg_dct.h,
     tests/t41/avc_import_test.c, tests/t41/core_lease_test.c
   - GPL-2.0: tests/t41/v4l2_avc_test.c (test program only, not part of
     libimp)
   - GPL-2.0-or-later: src/t30/h264enc/ (derived from x264, Copyright (C)
     2003-2014 x264 project; see the headers of cabac.c, set.h, slice.h,
     bitstream.h).  These files are built into the T21, T23 and T30
     libimp.so, so those binaries carry GPL-2.0-or-later obligations.
   - BSD-3-Clause: src/audio/webrtc/ (third-party, see below).

2. Files without a license header carry no explicit license grant.  They
   remain the copyright of their authors (see `git log`).  Ask the
   authors before redistributing them under specific terms.

The repository also stores reverse-engineering notes and dumps of the
vendor binary (e.g. docs/re/libimp.so_hlil.txt).  These are documentation of the
vendor ABI and are not compiled into libimp.

